    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0971" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p1/pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.00/1–454</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d493-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1954-01-04">January 4,
                            1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <note rend="inline" type="source">[Extract]</note>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Senator George brought up Indochina. He was greatly worried
                    about that situation. He hopes that no effort will be made to get Congress’ <pb
                        facs="0972" n="940" xml:id="pg940"/> consent to sending in U.S. troops. We
                    talked about possible sea and air activity, to which he did not seem seriously
                    to object.</p>
                <p>. . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d493-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d493-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Secretary Dulles.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
